      "title": "👈 Models",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Select your preferred Wan VACE, CLIP and VAE models\n> - Select a VACE model of the same model type and quantization that you run in your regular Wan generation workflow. If you usually run FP8 for video generation, choose FP8 VACE models. If you usually use Q4 GGUF, use Q4 GGUF VACE models.\n> - *The key to success and no OOM is to configure this workflow as close to your regular Wan workflow as possible.*\n> - **If you need GGUF models, replace these nodes with your favorite GGUF loaders.**\n"
      ],
      "color": "#233",
      "bgcolor": "#355"
    },
    {
      "id": 73,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -2840,
        2000
      ],
      "size": [
        380,
        190
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 10,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "👆Speedup Loras",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Select Lightning/Lightx2v Loras\n> - Loras are enabled by default because that seems to be how most people do Wan generation.\n> - For best results, use the same lora models and lora strength that your input clips were generated with.\n> - Reducing lora strength or disabling the loras completely can reduce color/brightness artifacts.\n> - If you disable loras, don't forget to adjust sampler settings appropriately. See the **Samplers** note below."
      ],
      "color": "#233",
      "bgcolor": "#355"
    },
    {
      "id": 74,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -3590,
        2750
      ],
      "size": [
        380,
        310
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 11,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "VACE Parameters 👆",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "**The defaults, `context_frames=8` and `replace_frames=8` usually work well for most 16 fps videos.**\n> - **extend_from_idx**: New frames will be generated from this point in the input video.\n> - **context_frames**: The number of reference frames immediately preceding `extend_from_idx` to use for generation context.\n> - **new_frames**: the number of brand new frames to generate.\n\nThis workflow will generate `context_frames + new_frames` frames at `extend_from_idx`.  \nOriginal frames that follow `extend_from_idx` will be discarded and replaced by `new_frames`.  \n `context_frames` mirror existing frames from the input video."
      ],
      "color": "#233",
      "bgcolor": "#355"
    },
    {
      "id": 75,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -2380,
        2390
      ],
      "size": [
        310,
        290
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 12,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "👈 Samplers",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Sampler settings\n\nInference parameters aren't any different from normal Wan 2.2 generation. If you have a favorite sampler/scheduler combination for Wan generation, it will probably work fine here.\n\n> The default values assume the speedup lora is active.\n> - `steps: 4`\n> - `cfg: 1.0`\n\n> Without loras, use higher values.\n> - `steps: 20`\n> - `cfg: 3.5`\n\n\n"
      ],
      "color": "#233",
      "bgcolor": "#355"
    },
